[33mcommit 30b3c54ddaa05f1486210c08d628269555383dd5[m
Author: Albert Elias <albertel1996@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 10:55:26 2026 +0200

    Vectorize the field calculation and add command-line options
    
    - schmidt.py: potentialfunction computes the whole (r, theta, phi) grid at
      once with matrix products instead of a Python loop over every point, the
      external field uses the same function (external=True) and totalfield
      adds internal and external fields and the modulus
    - reader.py: one generic read_table for all the tables, paths relative to
      the code (it can run from any folder), planet_settings with the size,
      default degree and units of each model, and the choice of the maximum
      degree and of the external field
    - Cartesian components and Brms are vectorized (Brms is now the true root
      mean square, and fieldx/fieldy used phi[j] instead of phi[k])
    - main.py, main_movie.py and main_movie_Earth.py take the planet, year,
      radius/radii, number of multipoles, external field, resolution, title
      and magnitude as arguments, with copy-paste examples in --help
    - The movie scripts print the ffmpeg commands for the movie and its
      reverse
    - README updated with the new options
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

